A strange thing happened the other day; I took the stairs down from a level
in the 20's and ended up on a maze level that was not hell, with upgoing
and downgoing stairs! The next level was also a maze level, and then a
few normal levels before I reached the castle level. Has this happened
to anybody else?

On the subject of Stormbringer, remember that draining levels from your
opponent reduces the likelihood that you will get useful intrinsics by
eating its corpse... My first winning game was with a rustproof +7 Orcrist;
I spent my wishes on blessed potions of gain ability, +4 gauntlets of
dexterity, +4 helm of brilliance and an amulet of life saving (contrary
to a recent post, nothing funny happened when I wished for that). I
didn't bother wishing for Stormy, and I probably never will. Sure, it's
fun getting the life draining message, but I don't think it's worth it.

I'm all for a mall level, but I think robbing shops should send soldiers,
not Kops after you. Moreover, killing a shopkeeper should also cause 
soldiers to appear. Otherwise the whole level would be much too easy to
take advantage of. This level would favor lawful behavior, which would
be nice. Already, lawful characters are much harder to play than chaotics;
this would even the score a bit.

Stephane the former priest gone barbarian.





